{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions","id":1445213,"title":"[TC: Adventure! - Kickstarter] Impressions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-21T21:18:41-07:00","id":1445213,"title":"[TC: Adventure! - Kickstarter] Impressions","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Things I liked:</b></span><ul><li>The statement that Telluric energy is formed by Quantum and Psi \u201cglued\u201d by Flux is quite elegant.</li> </ul><ul><li>The explanation of the extension of Mercer's powers is very good. The narrative of the disaster and the time travel, is so cool. Possible mechanics of time travelling are promising.</li> </ul><ul><li>Showing Donighal flirting with Nazism, I think it works very well with the dissociation of humanity, inherent in the all Novas.</li> </ul><ul><li>The addition and contextualization of Sara Kaur, for me, was one of the greatest successes of this second edition.</li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Things I didn't like:</span></b><ul><li>The lack of the terms \u201cParamorph\u201d, \u201cEximorph\u201d... I love those terms. It gave a technical and scientific outlook to the Inspired, they fit perfectly with Primoris' scientific vision. (sci-fi lover detected).</li> </ul><ul><li>The explanation of the behavior of telluric energy. Where it says that Earth Energy exists in a state of fluctuation, that when it is appeased it is possible to harness the energy. In this part in particular I prefer the old version, which was related to the zero point energy theory (Z-rays). Which is a form of stasis energy, which, when excited, generates A LOT of energy and strange effects such as the creation of virtual matter, etc. This energy permeates the entire universe is a great basis for telluric anergy. It may have been just the author's semantics ... but I still prefer the old semantics <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . (sci-fi lover detected).</li> </ul><ul><li>I am confused if the Doyen barrier that was broken in N-Day surrounds only planet Earth or the entire Solar System. I may be mistaken, but all references in the other books portray the barrier only around planet Earth, so, which one is correct?</li> </ul><ul><li>The fact that there were Inspired and Strange Places before the Hammesmith event. In my opinion, this dissociates the game world even more from our own, and also diminishes the importance of the Hammesmith event. I understand that this and the introduction of the Esoteric Order of the \u00c6ons in canon is probably an editorial decision to launch new game lines; I understand that\u2026 but I don't like it.</li> </ul><ul><li>And finally ... Max's feelings for Michael .... You see, in my opinion, the best character in the whole Trinity Continuum is Michael Donighal / Michael Daemon / Doctor Primoris / Divis Mal. His evolution from a simple human to a god is simply awesome, and better yet, it\u2019s totally credible. Also, the fact that this character is gay, and has romantic feelings unrequited by Max Mercer (his best friend), gives the character even more depth, because despite having all the power in the world, all his transcendence, he doesn't have the love of the one person he loved. (at least not in the way Michael wanted).<br /> <br /> That said, I think the new alternative, where Mercer also loves (romantically) Michael, lessens the impact of the two characters' story. The Divis Mal tragedy becomes a little less... &quot;tragic&quot; \u2013 for his romantic love is at least reciprocated (even if the sexual component isn\u2019t). As for Mercer, it seems a little sadistic, boastful or stupid on his part, to not have a relationship with the person he loves because he doesn\u2019t see himself as the ideal partner for Michael. During the Aberrant timeline, Scripture tells us that Divis Mal transcended his sexual desires (or at least doesn\u2019t pursue them anymore), even if they still maintain their love, so why wouldn\u2019t Max have a romantic relationship with Mal in similar terms? Finally, I always thought of Max Mercer as the quintessential Pulp hero, \u201cloved by women, a lover to them, and respected by men\u201d, whilst still maintaining a progressive spirit for his time (despite this concept being dated, maybe even for a Pulp game). This new take on the character, in my view, does not fit very well with the concept of Pulp hero... but I may be wrong. Still, I didn't like this reimagination so much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ul><br /> \u200bI would like to know your impressions of the game. I liked a lot of things, others not so much, I would like to know your opinion.<br /> <br /> There was another topic I intended to use, for this post, but it was closed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26537,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","user":"Jonnes.Derik","date":". 04-22-2021, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T22:39:42-07:00","id":1445223,"title":"","content":"As an ACE nothing rings truer than Max's actions. And this is in the modern 21st century. I can't imagine being a ACE in the 20s. I spent a Noninsignificant portion of my life wondering if was broken. It wasn't until I found the term on the internet that I could wrap myself around it. So yeah thinking &quot;I can't give you what you need and I care too much to hurt you&quot; makes perfect sense to me. <br /> <br /> So does Michael's response &quot;who are you to decide for me!&quot; Its a much more interesting tragedy to me than &quot;Oh he just had a crush on a straight man&quot; but then as an ACE I can relate to the whole thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T22:43:58-07:00","id":1445225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions#post1445213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]The fact that there were Inspired and Strange Places before the Hammesmith event. In my opinion, this dissociates the game world even more from our own, and also diminishes the importance of the Hammesmith event. I understand that this and the introduction of the Esoteric Order of the \u00c6ons in canon is probably an editorial decision to launch new game lines; I understand that\u2026 but I don't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1E explanation works quite well. The Hammersmith explosion also had waves that went backwards in time and released bits of it then.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T07:43:32-07:00","id":1445262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions#post1445213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[SIZE=20px][*]The lack of the terms \u201cParamorph\u201d, \u201cEximorph\u201d... I love those terms. It gave a technical and scientific outlook to the Inspired, they fit perfectly with Primoris' scientific vision. (sci-fi lover detected).</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in 1e, those terms weren't developed until much later (chronologically the first time we saw them was in a Babel Dossier document from 1998, as seen in the Aberrant Players Guide).<br /> <br /> Mesmerist, daredevil, and stalwart are genre-appropriate terms, and it won't be another few decades before the -morph terminology is developed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that there were Inspired and Strange Places before the Hammesmith event. In my opinion, this dissociates the game world even more from our own, and also diminishes the importance of the Hammesmith event. I understand that this and the introduction of the Esoteric Order of the \u00c6ons in canon is probably an editorial decision to launch new game lines; I understand that\u2026 but I don't like it. </div> </div> </div>Again, this is present in 1e. The sidebar on p. 216 points out that Z-waves propagate forward and backward in time. The Inspirations section on p. 265 even refers to this sidebar as the excuse STs need to run <i>The Mummy</i> with a clear conscience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And finally ... Max's feelings for Michael .... </div> </div> </div>&quot;Gay man has unrequited feelings for a straight man&quot; is a pretty overused trope at this point, and we wanted something deeper. As others have pointed out, many readers are identifying with the characters in a way they didn't before, and that's important to us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, I always thought of Max Mercer as the quintessential Pulp hero, \u201cloved by women, a lover to them, and respected by men\u201d, whilst still maintaining a progressive spirit for his time (despite this concept being dated, maybe even for a Pulp game). This new take on the character, in my view, does not fit very well with the concept of Pulp hero... but I may be wrong. Still, I didn't like this reimagination so much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Pulp stories were rooted in the cultural mores of the time, many of which were, frankly, garbage. I'm sorry you don't enjoy the new take on their relationship. I would suggest you expand your definition of pulp hero, but in any case it's trivial for you to rewrite Max or Primoris for your own games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:10:59-07:00","id":1445333,"title":"","content":"If the definition of quintessential pulp hero precludes certain marginalized sexual orientations (asexual in this case) then the definition of quintessential pulp hero is clearly in need of forcible expanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T15:16:39-07:00","id":1445353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445333#post1445333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the definition of quintessential pulp hero precludes certain marginalized sexual orientations (asexual in this case) then the definition of quintessential pulp hero is clearly in need of forcible expanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea that the 'pulp hero' excludes asexuals is weird as so many pulp heroes were written as if they were asexual. This was accidental, I assume, but typical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T19:35:15-07:00","id":1445399,"title":"","content":"Between you and me, most of the pulp characters have no sexual orientation at all, we suppose they are straight because it\u2019s the \u201cnormal\u201d, but you see no sexual or even romantic relationship. Yes there are some that are, as said, \u201cloved by women and respected by men\u201d, and some that are as sexualized as a family guy (having kids don\u2019t prove more than a few times it worked for the couple). You can see Batman (at least before JL) as an Ace that pretends to be attracted to women to fit society, the same way he pretend to care about the high society futilities.<br /> <br /> Pretending to be something is not a social media thing, there was always people pretending to be what they were not, even people that would accept themselves as gay if had the chance, fight their own selves to fit the expectations, some turned violently, angry with the world and their families, others become apathetic, and some had secret lives. Women were in a even worse position, some, even if not LGBT+, where traumatized by their husbands sexual approaches and had their libido treated as an enemy instead of part of themselves.<br /> <br /> Well, it didn\u2019t change that much in the last 100 years...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T11:37:33-07:00","id":1445504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even in 1e, those terms weren't developed until much later (chronologically the first time we saw them was in a Babel Dossier document from 1998, as seen in the Aberrant Players Guide). Mesmerist, daredevil, and stalwart are genre-appropriate terms, and it won't be another few decades before the -morph terminology is developed </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, this is present in 1e. The sidebar on p. 216 points out that Z-waves propagate forward and backward in time. The Inspirations section on p. 265 even refers to this sidebar as the excuse STs need to run The Mummy with a clear conscience. </div> </div> </div>I reviewed the material you indicated, and now I understand the proposal, it seems like a really good explanation. I have to analyze the implications of this in my continuum, with respect to chance and paradoxes, to keep my timeline more cohesive and without plot holes as much as possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cPulp stories were rooted in the cultural mores of the time, many of which were, frankly, garbage.\u201d </div> </div> </div>I agree with that. But here is a better way to deepen my point of view.<br /> <br /> See, let's take H.P Lovecraft as an example as a contemporary personality from the 20s and 30s, whose work is loved by many, but which is nevertheless extremely racist. Unfortunately, such postures were socially accepted and common in that period. It is obvious and clear that I abhor racism, homophobia, misogyny, and any form of segregation and social repression, and I am extremely happy that these problems are faced openly today. I think that all representativeness is important.<br /> <br /> That said, as for fictional and entertainment works, I tend to prefer characters that are in some way, a representation of their own time. Although these characters are imperfect by today's standards.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Mercer, as a character, in my opinion, should better portray the spirit, genre / era of the game, since he is the guiding thread of this specific scenario (just as Divis Mal is the guiding thread of Aberrant and Sara Kaur is Aeon's). When I mentioned the characteristic \u201cloved by women, a lover to them, and respected by men\u201d. I don't think it should be extolled as a virtue. Certainly, it is a posture that raises questions regarding the objectification of women and so on. But still, even though it is a character flaw, it should still be a possible feature of Mercer. Which, in my opinion, would enrich the character, placing him as a contemporary of the twentieth century.<br /> <br /> See, I think Emperor Palpatine (Darth Sidious) is one of the best characters in Star Wars. But I am not in favor of authoritarian, homicidal, fascist attitudes and so on. However, these characteristics make him a very interesting character.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gay man has unrequited feelings for a straight man&quot; is a pretty overused trope at this point, and we wanted something deeper. As others have pointed out, many readers are identifying with the characters in a way they didn't before, and that's important to us. </div> </div> </div>I think here, my argument has been reduced to just <i>&quot;Gay man has unrequited feelings for a straight man &quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> Well, in that regard, I like to think of Michael Donighal / Divis Mal, as a tragic character in many ways. The main one being the fact that even though it is the most powerful entity on earth it is simply IMPOSSIBLE that your loved one will return your love in the same way.<br /> <br /> For me, situations that harmonize with these personal tragedies, greatly increase the quality of the character, in the same way that situations that decrease this point make the character and the backstory more vapid. I have no problem with Mercer being asexual, however the fact that he reciprocates Michael's feelings lessens the dramatic burden and potency of the Divis Mal tragedy, because in this scenario, a romantic relationship is possible.<br /> <br /> In addition to causing a certain contradiction with what is said in TC: Aberrant, where it implies that in the New Era, Divis Mal transcended his need for carnal love, as we can see in the evolution of his relationship with Scripture. Nothing prevents Divis from having the same kind of relationship with Mercer. After all, if we take for granted that Mercer is in love with Mal (given that he is an ACE, but with homo-romantic feelings for Michael), they could be together in these terms, without any problem in the Aberrant era. Why don't they do it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sorry you don't enjoy the new take on their relationship. </div> </div> </div>That\u00b4s ok... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would suggest you expand your definition of pulp hero </div> </div> </div>You are probably right.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but in any case it's trivial for you to rewrite Max or Primoris for your own games. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I will do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore, thank you very much for answering and clarifying some points. If possible I would like some clarification regarding the Doyen barrier.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am confused if the Doyen barrier that was broken in N-Day surrounds only planet Earth or the entire Solar System. I may be mistaken, but all references in the other books portray the barrier only around planet Earth, so, which one is correct? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T11:43:32-07:00","id":1445506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445333#post1445333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the definition of quintessential pulp hero precludes certain marginalized sexual orientations (asexual in this case) then the definition of quintessential pulp hero is clearly in need of forcible expanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T11:48:31-07:00","id":1445507,"title":"","content":"I would say that if you're going to have an interplanetary adventure, then The shield was around the entire solar system. If you're restricting your adventures just to the planet Earth then the barrier was just around the planet Earth. <br /> <br /> It's essentially an issue of \u201cwherever your Inspired go, they're within the shield\u201d. This is because, as was revealed near the end of the mysteriously closed thread, that barrier is the reason why stalwarts are stalwarts and not Novas. And this in turn means that if a stalwort somehow finds himself outside the barrier, he may turn into a Nova.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-23-2021, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T11:52:34-07:00","id":1445509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445504#post1445504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I reviewed the material you indicated, and now I understand the proposal, it seems like a really good explanation. I have to analyze the implications of this in my continuum, with respect to chance and paradoxes, to keep my timeline more cohesive and without plot holes as much as possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree with that. But here is a better way to deepen my point of view.<br /> <br /> See, let's take H.P Lovecraft as an example as a contemporary personality from the 20s and 30s, whose work is loved by many, but which is nevertheless extremely racist. Unfortunately, such postures were socially accepted and common in that period. It is obvious and clear that I abhor racism, homophobia, misogyny, and any form of segregation and social repression, and I am extremely happy that these problems are faced openly today. I think that all representativeness is important.<br /> <br /> That said, as for fictional and entertainment works, I tend to prefer characters that are in some way, a representation of their own time. Although these characters are imperfect by today's standards.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Mercer, as a character, in my opinion, should better portray the spirit, genre / era of the game, since he is the guiding thread of this specific scenario (just as Divis Mal is the guiding thread of Aberrant and Sara Kaur is Aeon's). When I mentioned the characteristic \u201cloved by women, a lover to them, and respected by men\u201d. I don't think it should be extolled as a virtue. Certainly, it is a posture that raises questions regarding the objectification of women and so on. But still, even though it is a character flaw, it should still be a possible feature of Mercer. Which, in my opinion, would enrich the character, placing him as a contemporary of the twentieth century.<br /> <br /> See, I think Emperor Palpatine (Darth Sidious) is one of the best characters in Star Wars. But I am not in favor of authoritarian, homicidal, fascist attitudes and so on. However, these characteristics make him a very interesting character.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think here, my argument has been reduced to just <i>&amp;quot;Gay man has unrequited feelings for a straight man &amp;quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> Well, in that regard, I like to think of Michael Donighal / Divis Mal, as a tragic character in many ways. The main one being the fact that even though it is the most powerful entity on earth it is simply IMPOSSIBLE that your loved one will return your love in the same way.<br /> <br /> For me, situations that harmonize with these personal tragedies, greatly increase the quality of the character, in the same way that situations that decrease this point make the character and the backstory more vapid. I have no problem with Mercer being asexual, however the fact that he reciprocates Michael's feelings lessens the dramatic burden and potency of the Divis Mal tragedy, because in this scenario, a romantic relationship is possible.<br /> <br /> In addition to causing a certain contradiction with what is said in TC: Aberrant, where it implies that in the New Era, Divis Mal transcended his need for carnal love, as we can see in the evolution of his relationship with Scripture. Nothing prevents Divis from having the same kind of relationship with Mercer. After all, if we take for granted that Mercer is in love with Mal (given that he is an ACE, but with homo-romantic feelings for Michael), they could be together in these terms, without any problem in the Aberrant era. Why don't they do it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That\u00b4s ok... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You are probably right.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, I will do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore, thank you very much for answering and clarifying some points. If possible I would like some clarification regarding the Doyen barrier.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Max is a protagonist. You don\u2019t want your protagonist to exemplify cis male heterosexist stereotypes. Personally once I thought about it I really liked the new Max/Michael romance storyline. But like Ian said you can always change it back to the old version in your campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T12:02:07-07:00","id":1445511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445504#post1445504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to causing a certain contradiction with what is said in TC: Aberrant, where it implies that in the New Era, Divis Mal transcended his need for carnal love, as we can see in the evolution of his relationship with Scripture. Nothing prevents Divis from having the same kind of relationship with Mercer. After all, if we take for granted that Mercer is in love with Mal (given that he is an ACE, but with homo-romantic feelings for Michael), they could be together in these terms, without any problem in the Aberrant era. Why don't they do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if you've ever been in a relationship that's gone south before, but by the time of Aberrant, Max and Mal have a literal CENTURY of bad blood and resentment. The initial roadblock to their relationship may be gone, but there's now a cliff wall in its place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, thank you very much for answering and clarifying some points. If possible I would like some clarification regarding the Doyen barrier. </div> </div> </div>I didn't answer because I didn't see it as relevant. The Doyen barrier is designed to impact humanity, and it breaks in 2018. Whether that barrier is surrounding Earth or the solar system doesn't really impact that goal, because other than a bare handful of humans that went to the Moon, every single human in that time period remained on Earth.<br /> <br /> So the answer is whatever makes things more interesting for your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T12:18:27-07:00","id":1445512,"title":"","content":"Not disagreeing with the changes in question (I'm fine with it either way), but if a particular cis white hetero male stereotype is not offensive, what's wrong with using it? Specifically, I'm referring to Penelope's comment that it being a cis white hetero male stereotype is <i>in and of itself</i> enough of a reason not to do it.<br /> <br /> Again, I fully get Ian's interest in going a different direction this time around; and to me, that's a good enough reason to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T12:35:58-07:00","id":1445516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445512#post1445512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not disagreeing with the changes in question (I'm fine with it either way), but if a particular cis white hetero male stereotype is not offensive, what's wrong with using it? Specifically, I'm referring to Penelope's comment that it being a cis white hetero male stereotype is <i>in and of itself</i> enough of a reason not to do it.<br /> <br /> Again, I fully get Ian's interest in going a different direction this time around; and to me, that's a good enough reason to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was about to write the same comment. Being a heterosexual white man don\u2019t make you the enemy or evil, not even a simplistic or bad character, as long he is not an asshole it\u2019s ok.<br /> <br /> Max is kind of an asshole (the 3 from the Trinity are) probably not in the same scale as Mal (come on, Mal has Mega Ego 5+), but they are prepotent, manipulative and try to reach their own agendas at any cost, even if it\u2019s a good agenda in the end...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T12:50:00-07:00","id":1445522,"title":"","content":"There's nothing wrong with white, cis, hetero men. (At least I hope not; I am one.) However, if there is already a white, cis, hetero character taking up space which could be used to give someone else a voice or representation, then I'd prefer the white straight guy not be the one to get the slot. I can see white straight male characters all over the place. Others don't necessarily get to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T13:39:27-07:00","id":1445528,"title":"","content":"Considering Adventure! has a strong gay male character and a strong female character there totally should be a strong straight male character. That way everyone can find someone they see in the story. Michael is gay, Sara is a strong woman, and Max is a straight male. Nothing wrong with that. <br /> <br /> And I am speaking as a gay man. <br /> <br /> Also, the whole 'one sided love between a gay man and a straight guy' might be a trope, but its a trope for a reason - it happens, its real. So it shouldn't simply be ignored just because its been done. <br /> <br /> Max having a woman at every port but no true love is not something bad to me, especially when we have Michael as a gay man to be an icon too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T13:49:56-07:00","id":1445531,"title":"","content":"Well, in the long run, the gay man becomes a villain and the strong women is dominated... so... complex situation...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T13:58:43-07:00","id":1445534,"title":"","content":"Good point there. That said I don't really consider the gay man as a villain because his whole point was 'novas are different and thus should be held to a different standard then baselines' which I don't entirely see as a wrong or bad thing. As for the other, what happened to her is bad, like really bad, but at least in the end she managed to manipulate things and broke free. That said her going from Psiad to Psion is a kick and a punishment and it really annoys me that the Doyen hamstrung her powers that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:09:00-07:00","id":1445538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445522#post1445522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing wrong with white, cis, hetero men. (At least I hope not; I am one.) However, if there is already a white, cis, hetero character taking up space which could be used to give someone else a voice or representation, then I'd prefer the white straight guy not be the one to get the slot. I can see white straight male characters all over the place. Others don't necessarily get to.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if you take that to its logical extreme, you end up without any slots for white het cis males. <br /> <br /> And that's a common complaint these days, that efforts to increase diversity have gone overboard to the point that the only slots left for white het cis males are the punching bags and the villains. <br /> <br /> Not that that's a problem TC:A! has, mind you; there are several other members of the \u00c6on Society who are white het cis male heroes. Again, I'm not objecting to the change that was made. Just an observation of where others have gone wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:12:49-07:00","id":1445539,"title":"","content":"Not exactly the logical conclusion, since the intent is to make room for those not represented. If the white, cis, straight man is no longer represented, the rubric would demand you make room for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:26:56-07:00","id":1445542,"title":"","content":"To be clear, you suggested that if there's a slot that can be filled either with a white het cis male or someone else, it should go to someone else. Applying that rule uniformly would remove all white het cis males. And in practice, there have been cases where the only slots left are the ones that paint the character in a bad light; because who wants to be accused of being disrespectful to minorities? <br /> <br /> But yeah; I have no problem with such a rule being applied in moderation. And we should probably cut it here, as this actually isn't an issue with this particular product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-23-2021, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:51:11-07:00","id":1445547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, in the long run, the gay man becomes a villain and the strong women is dominated... so... complex situation... </div> </div> </div>so ... I have NEVER seen Divis Mal like a villain. I have always seen him as a spirit of freedom taken to the last consequences. He has his flaws, but not necessarily villainous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik","name":"Jonnes.Derik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26537_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:52:32-07:00","id":1445548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445511#post1445511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't answer because I didn't see it as relevant. The Doyen barrier is designed to impact humanity, and it breaks in 2018. Whether that barrier is surrounding Earth or the solar system doesn't really impact that goal, because other than a bare handful of humans that went to the Moon, every single human in that time period remained on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the relevance is about the &quot;little green men of Mars&quot; or the &quot;Venusian civilization&quot; and the like, especially during Adventure's timeline. If I want to have &quot;green martians&quot; in my Adventure games (and to explore their homeworld cities with my Daredevil astronauts), should I set Mars/Venus inside or outside the Doyen barrier? \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> Besides that, AEON tells us that the Doyen also try to control any Alien civilizations that start to show Psionic (or Quantum) powers: in these cases (extrasolar Aliens), should we admit that the Doyen have a Barrier outside their planet, or no? \ud83e\udd14<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T15:49:45-07:00","id":1445560,"title":"","content":"As I said before, inside. If it was outside, not only would you likely be dealing with Talents, Novas, and psiads rather than daredevils, stalwarts, and mesmerists, but you also likely wouldn't have martians or cytherians. In both cases, it's the interaction between the Hammersmith event and the Doyen shield that causes the Adventure era telluric energies to have the properties that they have, including the spawning of strange places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-23-2021, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T22:30:18-07:00","id":1445609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonnes.Derik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445547#post1445547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> so ... I have NEVER seen Divis Mal like a villain. I have always seen him as a spirit of freedom taken to the last consequences. He has his flaws, but not necessarily villainous.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, he seems to be simply Nietzschean- the human is something to be exceeded, all previous values must be discarded and built anew, etc, etc. The big thing that probably establishes him as a villain in the minds of many is that baseline humanity isn't important to him- the self-actualization of Novas is, whether collectively or individually. <br /> <br /> This is perhaps most evident in his last statement: &quot;Your legacy is our future&quot;. That is, the <i>only</i> lasting thing of worth done by baseline humanity was producing Novas. <br /> <br /> If you think that empathetic concern and respecting the basic dignity of human beings is necessary to be good, he doesn't qualify even if he's not actively malign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T22:46:36-07:00","id":1445613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445548#post1445548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the relevance is about the &quot;little green men of Mars&quot; or the &quot;Venusian civilization&quot; and the like, especially during Adventure's timeline. If I want to have &quot;green martians&quot; in my Adventure games (and to explore their homeworld cities with my Daredevil astronauts), should I set Mars/Venus inside or outside the Doyen barrier? \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>In the era of the game, there's no way to get a spacecraft to Mars or Venus by normal science. Anything that attempts it is going to be some sort of Inspiration-powered science, and once you fire that up, who knows where the spacecraft is going to wind up? If you had a super-science tunneling machine that drilled its way to a &quot;Hollow Earth&quot;, the Earth isn't hollow- the machine just wound up somewhere, probably one of those alternate places in the Continuum. An Inspired spacecraft that found Martians or Venereans probably went to another dimension entirely. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides that, AEON tells us that the Doyen also try to control any Alien civilizations that start to show Psionic (or Quantum) powers: in these cases (extrasolar Aliens), should we admit that the Doyen have a Barrier outside their planet, or no? \ud83e\udd14 </div> </div> </div>The Doyen seem to be amazingly scattershot in their handlings of other species- maybe to avoid looking like there's a pattern, maybe just because they're all at least two million years old and getting a little batty with age. Responses seem to have varied from &quot;obliterate them with asteroids&quot; to &quot;subvert the entire species and convince them they're noetically dumb&quot; to arranging alien invasions. Why Earth got a weird shield and not a repeat of the Chicxulub impactor, who knows? Could have just been the next strategy in the cardex or something the Doyen in charge of this part of space wanted to try and see if it worked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T01:28:46-07:00","id":1445628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445528#post1445528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering Adventure! has a strong gay male character and a strong female character there totally should be a strong straight male character. That way everyone can find someone they see in the story. Michael is gay, Sara is a strong woman, and Max is a straight male. Nothing wrong with that.<br /> <br /> And I am speaking as a gay man.<br /> <br /> Also, the whole 'one sided love between a gay man and a straight guy' might be a trope, but its a trope for a reason - it happens, its real. So it shouldn't simply be ignored just because its been done.<br /> <br /> Max having a woman at every port but no true love is not something bad to me, especially when we have Michael as a gay man to be an icon too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How about we keep Max Ace instead and not erase some of the very little represenation we get? Max as ACE makes sense. The situation with Michael very much hits home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T06:03:53-07:00","id":1445653,"title":"","content":"One thing we keep getting wrong about the Doyen is they are \u201cThe Doyen\u201d when they are actually a bunch of individuals with amazing Psionic powers and different plans for the universe and themselves.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut the Doyens would destroy earth to prevent Novas\u201d, yes, some of them would, but the ones that sensed the Hammersmith event didn\u2019t.<br /> \u201dIn Aeon they created the Psions, why didn\u2019t they create Psions to keep humans at bay in the Adventure era?\u201d Some created Psions, but some created the chromatics and start using Psions as warp drives against their will.<br /> <br /> They are just around, studying or doing nothing, or what ever an immortal being that need no sustenance and are immune to most of what the universe can throw at them do to pass their time, and they feel something, they don\u2019t come back to talk to their leader, they do something to prevent the issue from getting out of control, and than move on.<br /> <br /> In my head cannon they retired to throw asteroids against Earth during Nova Era, but, you know, Novas, they probably retired to aim a supernova against Earth and it didn\u2019t work too. Also in my head cannon, N-Day killed some Doyen that were around Earth, and that why they didn\u2019t react to the breach of their shield before, and when they did there were too many powerful quantum users to them to approach without risking their existence (they are immortal, they have a difference sense of time and urgency, even more for not knowing the responsible for that sector are dead).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T06:09:08-07:00","id":1445654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445653#post1445653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also in my head cannon, N-Day killed some Doyen that were around Earth, and that why they didn\u2019t react to the breach of their shield before, and when they did there were too many powerful quantum users to them to approach without risking their existence (they are immortal, they have a difference sense of time and urgency, even more for not knowing the responsible for that sector are dead).</div> </div> </div> </div>I may appropriate that one. Except that there was one Doyen monitoring the field. He had one job...let the other Doyen know if a lot of quantum energy was going to happen to that little third planet in that one system. Basically, the Doyen equivalent of manning a radar station in Alaska. This one Doyen thought &quot;Ok, so this one thing called the Galatea is just in near Earth orbit. No worries. I have time to go ahead and continue to develop a new color and....wait...who is that guy? What is he.....oh shiiiii.......&quot; and then he got obliterated in the resulting explosion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T06:19:51-07:00","id":1445656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445653#post1445653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing we keep getting wrong about the Doyen is they are \u201cThe Doyen\u201d when they are actually a bunch of individuals with amazing Psionic powers and different plans for the universe and themselves.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut the Doyens would destroy earth to prevent Novas\u201d, yes, some of them would, but the ones that sensed the Hammersmith event didn\u2019t.<br /> \u201dIn Aeon they created the Psions, why didn\u2019t they create Psions to keep humans at bay in the Adventure era?\u201d Some created Psions, but some created the chromatics and start using Psions as warp drives against their will.<br /> <br /> They are just around, studying or doing nothing, or what ever an immortal being that need no sustenance and are immune to most of what the universe can throw at them do to pass their time, and they feel something, they don\u2019t come back to talk to their leader, they do something to prevent the issue from getting out of control, and than move on.<br /> <br /> In my head cannon they retired to throw asteroids against Earth during Nova Era, but, you know, Novas, they probably retired to aim a supernova against Earth and it didn\u2019t work too. Also in my head cannon, N-Day killed some Doyen that were around Earth, and that why they didn\u2019t react to the breach of their shield before, and when they did there were too many powerful quantum users to them to approach without risking their existence (they are immortal, they have a difference sense of time and urgency, even more for not knowing the responsible for that sector are dead).</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here is something that has been bothering me for some time. On one hand The Doyen are described as a unified group trying to quash anything that could threaten them, while on the other they behave like a collective of individuals who, beyond survival (and they can't even agree how sometimes), don't really have any reason to be a society. I usually place them in the middle, but I would really like to see a supplement where we get to know their backstory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T06:23:26-07:00","id":1445658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445656#post1445656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I would really like to see a supplement where we get to know their backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you\u2019re in luck there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T08:34:49-07:00","id":1445669,"title":"","content":"I *really* hope you're talking about Under Alien Skies (thought it was Suns but MMN says Skies now) and not some other supplement coming much later. Progress indicates that book is getting quite close to publishing.<br /> <br /> Although I am excited for Mission Statements and giddy with anticipation for Prometheus Unbound, those seem to be quite some time before being finished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26269-bastion-avalos","name":"Bastion Avalos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T14:38:23-07:00","id":1445710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445654#post1445654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may appropriate that one. Except that there was one Doyen monitoring the field. He had one job...let the other Doyen know if a lot of quantum energy was going to happen to that little third planet in that one system. Basically, the Doyen equivalent of manning a radar station in Alaska. This one Doyen thought &quot;Ok, so this one thing called the Galatea is just in near Earth orbit. No worries. I have time to go ahead and continue to develop a new color and....wait...who is that guy? What is he.....oh shiiiii.......&quot; and then he got obliterated in the resulting explosion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have been even worse than that. There are at least 100 billion stars in our galaxy. Since only a subset of the Doyen race are likely to be on monitoring duty at any given time, every single active Doyen agent has to be monitoring dozens, hundreds, or even thousands of worlds. And if Doyen Agent X14785 misses his normal check-in, it may take awhile for them to track him down, especially if getting blown up by quantum power erased his noetic imprint, thereby making it impossible to simply use clairsentience.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T19:17:00-07:00","id":1445764,"title":"","content":"Transcendence makes you Asexual is not a good statement to have. Either you're saying sexuality is a base urge that can be transcended or that asexual people are tainted. So I am really glad Divis Mal is no longer &quot;beyond sexuality&quot;. Its not a cool tragic trope its... erasing a group and calling them inhuman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T19:20:48-07:00","id":1445765,"title":"","content":"I think, for Divis Mal, its not that he is 'beyond sexuality' he might just be beyond the need for physical sex. He still loves Scripture, who loves him. Meaning he is still gay. Still capable of romance and such. That said, maybe sex for him, at this point, is him and Scripture joining their essences in the universal consciousness or some other technobabble sort of way. Like they don't need the physical act because when they stare into each other's eyes their quantum signatures merge and they metaphysically explode in a way we baselines couldn't feel. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T19:34:20-07:00","id":1445767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445765#post1445765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, for Divis Mal, its not that he is 'beyond sexuality' he might just be beyond the need for physical sex. He still loves Scripture, who loves him. Meaning he is still gay. Still capable of romance and such. That said, maybe sex for him, at this point, is him and Scripture joining their essences in the universal consciousness or some other technobabble sort of way. Like they don't need the physical act because when they stare into each other's eyes their quantum signatures merge and they metaphysically explode in a way we baselines couldn't feel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ....everything about this is horrible. There are plenty of Asexual but romantics. There are plenty of demisexuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T22:49:14-07:00","id":1445782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445765#post1445765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He still loves Scripture, who loves him.</div> </div> </div> </div>WHAT?! \ud83d\ude32 Not knowing <b>Aberrant</b> good, I thought Scripture is book of Davis Mal movement, like <a href=\"https://www.gotquestions.org/names-titles-Bible.html\" target=\"_blank\">Bible title</a>. So it's Mal's modern lover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T05:34:21-07:00","id":1445808,"title":"","content":"Mal met Scripture as an Stalwart sometime between the end of Adventure era and many years before N-Day and become lovers. Scripture loves and worships Mal. He\u2019s name is Jeremiah Scripture, but it\u2019s probably not his original name.<br /> <br /> About sexual Mal, I agree with LordHeru, he is like a Tantra guru that can literally connect his energies to others and fulfill his sexual needs this way, he doesn\u2019t need his penis to full sexual pleasure, a Tantra guru can feel sexual pleasure from all their body, Mal can feel from all his quantum signature. He is not over sex, he is not ace, he is just don\u2019t need the bodily part of sex, he have sex in another level, he may be attracted sexually to Scripture and love him with all his soul, but they don\u2019t need the sexual intercourse to have sex, they can do it with their quantum signatures and all the technobabble...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 04-25-2021, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T07:30:48-07:00","id":1445818,"title":"","content":"Hmm. This is a very interesting discussion on the nature of Max Mercer, Michael Donighal, Sara Kaur and their influence on the Trinity Continuum setting. For my own take on things, I plan on treating this \u201cTelluric Triangle\u201d as merely one of many examples of characters in a vast multiverse, rather than the core of the setting. And it strikes me that this is what the core developers want to encourage anyway.<br /> <br /> Heck, I would LOVE to see some stories detailing other characters in the overall setting. Or even taking the many existing pulpy, proto-superhero tales in the public domain reworked for the Trinity Continuum. Anything to encourage creative chaos, and inspire (heh) creativity in Storytellers and players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T08:50:42-07:00","id":1445829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445808#post1445808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mal met Scripture as an Stalwart sometime between the end of Adventure era and many years before N-Day and become lovers. Scripture loves and worships Mal. He\u2019s name is Jeremiah Scripture, but it\u2019s probably not his original name.<br /> <br /> About sexual Mal, I agree with LordHeru, he is like a Tantra guru that can literally connect his energies to others and fulfill his sexual needs this way, he doesn\u2019t need his penis to full sexual pleasure, a Tantra guru can feel sexual pleasure from all their body, Mal can feel from all his quantum signature. He is not over sex, he is not ace, he is just don\u2019t need the bodily part of sex, he have sex in another level, he may be attracted sexually to Scripture and love him with all his soul, but they don\u2019t need the sexual intercourse to have sex, they can do it with their quantum signatures and all the technobabble...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you should look very hard at the implications of what this is saying unless you are going to argue for gender as written on the quantum level.. which is pretty damned extreme in the whole gender essentialism camp.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T09:19:47-07:00","id":1445834,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">I'm going to need everyone to dial this way back.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T09:21:42-07:00","id":1445835,"title":"","content":"This has nothing to do with gender or sexuality. A straight nova is still straight, a gay nova is still gay, an ace nova is still ace, a male nova is still male, a female nova is still female - plus all the other potentials that humanity can reach - all this is saying is that upon reaching the level of capability they have reached there is more to sex then simply the physical carnal aspect of it. I mean if two people could become one with the universe together then why would they just keep doing the old fashioned traditional sex. For them the definition of sex now equates to something much 'deeper', more cosmic. Something fueled by their quantum energies.<br /> <br /> This all said, when talking to baselines, I totally get them saying 'our relationship has gone beyond the sex that you know' because a nova like Divis Mal or Scripture isn't going to explain to a baseline the nature of reality or existence, or their interactions with it. They might explain such things to a Psiad, since I am pretty sure Divis Mal recognizes their equivalence, but not to a baseline.<br /> <br /> (I wrote this before seeing Ian's post)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T09:26:58-07:00","id":1445837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445818#post1445818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. This is a very interesting discussion on the nature of Max Mercer, Michael Donighal, Sara Kaur and their influence on the Trinity Continuum setting. For my own take on things, I plan on treating this \u201cTelluric Triangle\u201d as merely one of many examples of characters in a vast multiverse, rather than the core of the setting. And it strikes me that this is what the core developers want to encourage anyway.<br /> <br /> Heck, I would LOVE to see some stories detailing other characters in the overall setting. Or even taking the many existing pulpy, proto-superhero tales in the public domain reworked for the Trinity Continuum. Anything to encourage creative chaos, and inspire (heh) creativity in Storytellers and players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I think universes where one or more of them died or were not even present would be very interesting. I mean imagine a universe where Hammersmith himself doesn't die, just goes all something. It could be very interesting to see the potentials. <br /> <br /> That said, in some ways the only super essential person to the Adventure! timeline is Max - and that is because of him creating the Aeon Society. Michael and Sara, important in later games, aren't super necessary at this time. <br /> <br /> But, with that said, I do think they do have some cosmic weight to their natures. Maybe due to their essential actions later on or whatnot but I do think greater cosmology gives them a bit more oomph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T04:32:44-07:00","id":1445953,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to say that I liked all three of the Trinity as presented in the Kickstarter (Max, Michael and Sara).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T04:50:03-07:00","id":1445955,"title":"","content":"My only complaint is that the new edition only spotlights the big three. Nothing at all about the other founders of the \u00c6on Society (unless I missed something?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T12:23:32-07:00","id":1446131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1445213-tc-adventure-kickstarter-impressions?p=1445955#post1445955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only complaint is that the new edition only spotlights the big three. Nothing at all about the other founders of the \u00c6on Society (unless I missed something?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. They're nowhere to be found in the manuscript we got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T07:22:37-07:00","id":1446284,"title":"","content":"Oh, I almost forgot: I got the impression that the manuscript uses the word &quot;Psion&quot; when it should be using &quot;Psiad&quot; instead. Maybe it's worth to take a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T14:47:49-07:00","id":1446495,"title":"","content":"Something I find interesting in the setting secrets was the mention that the Doyen Barrier suppresses the progression of Stalwarts and Mesmerists to becoming Novas and Psiads. In addition, it's stated that without the intervention of the big 3 figures and the breaking of the barrier, that it's possible that Talents would eventually develop into controlled, presumably Tier-3 forms. Going off of this, if Stalwarts and Mesmerists began to lean more into Flux than quantum and noetic, enough so that they became &quot;Tier 3 Inspired,&quot; would they lose their ability to use quantum and psionics and become pure Flux users, using Flux to simulate their prior gifts, or would they become their own unique Tier 3 template? I doubt we'll ever get the answer, but it's one that I certainly find interesting as a homebrew fiend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}